  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">MF5-04 Paediatric Critical Care Capacity Building Project in Papua New Guinea</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Royal Australasian College of Surgeons (RACS) will work with their in-country partners The Papua New Guinea Women Doctors Association (PNG-WDA), The Pediatric Society of Papua New Guinea (PS-PNG) and the Advanced Pediatric Life Support Faculty Papua New Guinea (APLS-PNG) to contribute to improved health outcomes for pediatric patients across Papua New Guinea (PNG) by providing comprehensive clinical training courses and gender awareness training.</narrative>
  </description>
